course: dictionary
lesson: 13114
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. «Sam wanted to get some money, so he decided to flog his old bike.» The clues are money and bike, so flog means sell. Always test your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: «Long ago, sailors who broke the rules were flogged with a whip.» The clue is the whip, so here flog means beat someone hard as a punishment. This is a cruel punishment from long ago, and it is now illegal in most places.
explain: Flog can also mean trying hard at something that will never work. «Tom kept arguing with his brother, even though he had already lost.» People say Tom is flogging a dead horse. A dead horse cannot be made to move, so the effort is wasted.
fact: Flog is a verb, so its forms are flog, flogs, flogged and flogging.
fact: In the UK and Australia, «flog» often means to sell something, usually quickly or cheaply.
fact: «Flog» can mean to beat someone hard with a whip or stick as a punishment, which is now illegal in most places.
fact: In Australian and New Zealand slang, «flog» can also mean to steal.
fact: «Flogging a dead horse» means wasting effort on something that will not work.
exercise: «Sam decided to flog his old bike for five pounds.» What does flog mean here? | To paint | To steal | To beat | *To sell
exercise: «The sailors long ago were flogged for breaking the rules.» What does flogged mean? | Sent home to rest | Taught to sail a boat | Given a prize for good work | *Beaten hard as a punishment
exercise: «Trying to make Sam agree now is like flogging a dead horse.» What does this phrase mean? | *Wasting effort on something that will not work | Riding a horse very fast | Feeding an old animal | Winning a race
test: «Mum said the shop had flogged all its old toys in one afternoon.» What does flogged mean? | Mended | Beaten | Hidden | *Sold quickly
test: In Australia, Jake says someone flogged his bike from the shed. What does flogged mean here? | Painted | Mended | Found | *Stole
exam: Which sentence uses flog to mean sell? | *«Ali wants to flog his old games console.» | «Dad said flogging a dead horse was silly.» | «The horse ran very fast.» | «The sailor was flogged long ago.»
